WHAT THIS IS, AND WHAT IT IS NOT
--------------------------------
This is NOT a verification result. Kani could not be installed (see
20260806-2310_kani_install_attempt.log). Every harness in this repository is NOT RUN.

What this log establishes is strictly weaker and strictly prior: whether the
`#[cfg(kani)]` harness code compiles at all. Kani front-ends rustc, so a harness
module that does not type-check can never be model-checked; `cargo kani` would abort
at codegen. Enabling the cfg by hand reproduces exactly the compilation Kani would
attempt, minus the `kani` crate itself (which Kani injects, and whose absence accounts
for the 21 E0433 `cannot find module or crate 'kani'` errors below — those are expected
and are NOT defects). Every other error IS a defect and would still be present under
a real Kani run.

