INTERPRETATION
--------------
`kani_proofs.rs` is stale with respect to this branch. `protocol/domain-separation`
added `trust_domain` / `trust_domains` / `delegation_depth` fields to EntityWire,
ResourceWire, ClaimWire, ActionWire and OwnershipRegistryWire; the harness helpers
(`human`, `machine`, `file_resource`, `claim`, `minimal_registry_with_owner`,
`base_action`, lines 17-78) were never updated. Because every harness in the file is
built from those helpers, ALL 20 harnesses in kani_proofs.rs fail to compile. The
breakage is invisible to `cargo build` and `cargo test` precisely because the module
is `#[cfg(kani)]`, and nothing in CI sets that cfg.

SEPARATE DEFECT: ORPHANED HARNESS FILES
---------------------------------------
Three files under authgate-kernel/src/tcb/ contain `#[kani::proof]` harnesses but are
not declared as modules anywhere. `authgate-kernel/src/tcb/mod.rs` declares only
call_gate, dag, types, engine, tests, hardening_tests. A repo-wide grep for the module
names returns zero hits:

  $ grep -rn "kani_chain\|kani_confinement" --include=*.rs --include=*.toml authgate-kernel/
  (no output)

Orphans, with the harnesses they contain:
  authgate-kernel/src/tcb/kani_chain.rs        proof_attenuation_two_node, proof_epoch_check
  authgate-kernel/src/tcb/kani_confinement.rs  proof_subject_resource_binding,
                                               proof_canonical_gate_completeness,
                                               proof_rights_sufficiency
  authgate-kernel/src/tcb/sequence.rs          prop_seq_accumulated_monotone,
                                               prop_seq_exceeds_limit_consistent,
                                               prop_seq_step_count_matches_records,
                                               prop_seq_empty_never_exceeds,
                                               prop_seq_idempotent_rights

Note authgate-kernel/src/sequence.rs (3525 bytes) is a DIFFERENT file from
authgate-kernel/src/tcb/sequence.rs (7591 bytes); lib.rs:11 `pub mod sequence;` binds the
former, which contains no harnesses. kani_chain.rs and kani_confinement.rs additionally
open with `use authgate_kernel::tcb::types::*;` -- an external-crate path that cannot
resolve from inside the crate -- so they would not compile even if declared.

These 10 harnesses are not in any compilation unit. `cargo kani` would not discover them.

A fourth file, formal/kani/prop_revocation.rs (proof_forged_revocation_ignored,
proof_epoch_gate_priority), sits outside the crate directory entirely and belongs to no
cargo target.

